      "type": "listening_script",
      "content": "Many of the foods we eat depend on bees. When bees visit flowers, they carry pollen from one flower to another. Apples, strawberries, and almonds need this help. Some crops, like rice and wheat, are pollinated by the wind, so they don't need bees. Sadly, the number of bees is decreasing. The loss of flowers, the use of pesticides, and climate change are some of the reasons. If we lose bees, our meals will become much less colorful.",
